From e410f5e5a41df48dea8004a70940b549d1eca5de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 04:18:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Stop replaying stale quotes as if they were live
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The index cards were showing prices that didn't match the real
market (e.g. NIFTY 50 frozen at a stale LTP/prev-close while the
actual index had moved on with the opposite sign of change).

Root cause: KiteFeed.get_live_quote() falls back to its in-memory
quote cache whenever the live Kite call fails, with no ceiling on
how old that cache is allowed to be. A persistent quote failure (not
just a one-off blip - transient ones are already retried 3x inside
_call) then replays the same old price forever. Worse,
get_index_snapshots() wrote a fresh IndexSnapshot row with
timestamp=now() on every cycle regardless of whether the quote
underneath it was actually fresh, so the dashboard's "last updated"
clock kept advancing on a price that had stopped moving - nothing
visible told you it was stale.

Fixes, in feed_kite.py / scanner.py / dashboard.py / templates:
- get_live_quote() now tracks when each cached quote was captured
  and only serves it as a fallback within QUOTE_CACHE_MAX_AGE_SECONDS
  (default 90s, config.py). Past that ceiling it raises instead of
  quietly serving an arbitrarily old price - a persistent failure now
  surfaces as a failure.
- Every quote is tagged stale=True/False so callers can tell a live
  print from a replayed one.
- get_index_snapshots() skips writing an index_snapshots row for a
  stale quote, so the last genuinely live row - and its real
  timestamp - stays in place instead of being overwritten with a
  falsely fresh one.
- The dashboard flags a card "STALE · HH:MM" (last real update time)
  once its snapshot is more than 150s old (2.5 missed 1-minute
  cycles) during a live session, instead of silently showing a
  frozen number as if current.

Verified with targeted tests: the cache-age ceiling (fresh cache
still serves stale=True, cache past the ceiling raises), that
get_index_snapshots() persists only the non-stale quote in a mixed
batch, and template rendering of the STALE badge - plus a clean run
of the existing selftest.py suite.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TTwCHXT3HSQFTa3kX6yUDc
